---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import { u } from '../lib/paths';
---

<Base
  title="Research"
  description="Research at the University of Mars, including the Jezero Observatory and undergraduate fellowships."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Research"
    title="Research"
    lede="Faculty research runs across the colleges. Undergraduates join labs, archives, and the observatory during the year and in summer."
    crumbs={[{ href: '/research/', label: 'Research' }]}
  >
    <p class="page-actions">
      <a class="btn" href="#undergraduate">Undergraduate fellowships</a>
    </p>
  </PageHero>
  <article class="prose wrap">
    <div class="media-block" id="observatory">
      <div class="frame">
        <Photo
          name="research"
          alt="Research building with a rooftop observatory dome at blue hour, beside a red plain."
          sizes="(min-width: 800px) 36rem, 100vw"
        />
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>Jezero Observatory</h2>
        <p>
          The observatory is a shared facility of the College of Science. It supports atmospheric measurement, geology
          field prep, and instrument courses. Public viewing nights are posted each month during the term. The building
          is not a museum; class and research time comes first.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="centers">Centers and institutes</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Center for Water and Climate, in the environmental engineering wing</li>
      <li>Institute for Public Health, shared with the College of Health</li>
      <li>Center for Teaching, which supports faculty course design</li>
      <li>University archives, in the library’s lower level</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="facilities">Core facilities</h2>
    <p>
      Shared labs include imaging, a machine shop, and a research greenhouse. A principal investigator requests time.
      Students do not book the machine shop directly; they work through a lab sponsor.
    </p>

    <h2 id="undergraduate">Undergraduate research</h2>
    <p>
      Summer Session 2027 fellowships are open now. The work lasts twelve weeks, carries a stipend, and does not have to
      be about this planet. Students in every college may apply. The deadline is Monday, February 1, 2027.
    </p>
    <p>
      Academic-year research is arranged with a faculty sponsor and can count as units. Credit is not the same as a
      fellowship, and a student may not be paid and earn units for the same hours.
    </p>
    <p><a href={u('/news/fellowships/')}>Fellowship announcement</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>
